    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF, 10-year horizon, scenario-weighted. Routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md row 2 (operating company, industrial/moderately cyclical) - Xylem is a pumps/treatment/metering manufacturer and services business whose value is its free cash flow; no bank/REIT/LIC/holdco features. No prior DCF and no MEMORY.md entry, so this is a fresh build. EBITDA BASIS: ebitda_margin_path is pre-SBC and on a CASH-CONVERSION basis, deliberately below the company's adjusted EBITDA margin (FY25 ~22.2%, FY26 guide 23.1-23.5%) and below GAAP EBITDA+SBC (FY25 20.5%). Reason: a GAAP component build of FY2025 gives ~$1.2bn of unlevered FCF against $910M reported; the ~$250M gap is recurring restructuring/special-charge cash, pension and other operating outflows that Xylem incurs every year (FY23-25 each show a $245-268M gap between NI+D&A+SBC and OCF). The year-1 margin of 18.5% is calibrated so FY2026 owner FCF (~$1.03bn, ~11.2% of revenue) sits just above FY2025's $842M owner FCF, consistent with H1-26 FCF +30% YoY. D&A: 6.4% of revenue in FY2025 is inflated by Evoqua acquired-intangible amortization; it glides to ~4.5% as that amortizes off, which raises the cash tax burden over time. WORKING CAPITAL: manufacturer, wc_capture negative (growth consumes ~18-20% of incremental revenue). PORTFOLIO MOVES: the pending Cornell/Roper Pump acquisition ($1.46bn, announced 2026-08-11) and WaterFleet (~$200M) are excluded from both the flows and the bridge (assumed bought at roughly NPV-neutral prices); the AURELIUS international-metering sale is reflected only via the FY2026 ~2% reported-growth guide. The Q2-26 debt rise to $2.93bn funded the H1-26 buyback and TriOS, and is in net debt. BUYBACKS: Xylem is now a genuine repurchaser ($1.24bn H1-26); per method they are value-neutral here, and the lower share count is captured in the anchor.",
